{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_spin_only_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_spin_only_split","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L215-L227","doc":"**Spin-only, under balancing.**  Spin braided by the Hecke relation at `q`, isospin at the\nclassical point `t = 1`: the split is `σ⁶ τ⁶ (q¹⁰ − q⁶) tr p tr p'`, i.e. `D/S = q⁴` — not the\n`q⁵ − q³` (`D/S = q²`) of the half-twist convention `θ_λ = q^{c(λ)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_transparent_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_transparent_iff","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L194-L213","doc":"**Transparency under the Hecke braiding is the classical point.**  The isospin full twist acts\ntrivially on both `(4,2)` and `(3,3)` iff `t² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_iso_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_iso_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L179-L192","doc":"**The isospin twist is channel-blind iff `t⁴ = 1`.**  Under the Hecke braiding at `t` and the\nJM spectrum, `i = i'` (for a non-zero strand scalar) holds exactly when `t⁴ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_same_parameter_no_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_same_parameter_no_split","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L166-L177","doc":"**One Hecke braiding on both factors forces `D = S`.**  The corpus grades isospin by the\nHecke projectors of the same `H_n(q)` that carry spin; with `t = q`, balancing kills the split\nwhatever the strand scalars.  So `θ_iso = 1` is inconsistent with the ribbon axioms there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_balanced_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.hecke_balanced_split","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L149-L164","doc":"**Both factors braided by the Hecke relation, at parameters `q` (spin) and `t` (isospin).**\nGiven the Jucys–Murphy spectrum on each block (the corpus's named, cited open input), balancing\ngives `D − S = σ⁶ τ⁶ q⁶ t⁶ (q⁴ − t⁴) tr p tr p'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.theta_four_two_sq_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.theta_four_two_sq_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L140-L145","doc":"**The balancing ratio is `q⁴`, not `q²`.**  With the corpus identification\n`Δ²|_λ = θ_λ²`, the full-twist scalar on `(4,2)` is `q⁴` times that on `(3,3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.theta_three_three_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.theta_three_three_sq","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L134-L138","doc":"`θ_{(3,3)}² = x⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.theta_four_two_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.theta_four_two_sq","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L128-L132","doc":"`θ_{(4,2)}² = x¹⁰`: the full-twist scalar on `(4,2)` under the JM spectrum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.transparent_iso_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.transparent_iso_split","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L111-L120","doc":"**Transparent isospin derives the spin-only form.**  If the isospin monodromy is trivial, the\nfull twist acts by `1` on both isospin blocks; balancing then makes the isospin twist the single\nscalar `τ⁶`, and the split is `τ⁶ (s − s') tr p tr p'` — the shape of `spin_only_twist_split`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.balanced_iso_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.balanced_iso_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L100-L109","doc":"**The isospin twist is channel-blind iff its full twist is.**  A spin-only split needs only\n`i = i'` (then `D − S = i (s − s') tr p tr p'`).  Under balancing, `i = i'` holds exactly when the\nisospin full-twist scalars agree; the strand scalar `τ` cannot supply it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.balanced_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinTwistFromBalancing.balanced_split","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinTwistFromBalancing.lean#L89-L98","doc":"**Both factors balanced.**  Spin twist eigenvalues `s = σ⁶ g`, `s' = σ⁶ g'` and isospin twist\neigenvalues `i = τ⁶ f`, `i' = τ⁶ f'` (balancing on six strands: strand scalar to the sixth times\nthe full-twist scalar on the block).  The strand scalars factor out of the split. ","signatureChunk":0}]}